<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Home-screen sizes for the listings widget, in the launcher's own grid units.

  Every value is `70 × cells − 30` dp, the conversion the App Widget sizing guide gives for
  turning a cell count into the `minWidth` / `minHeight` a provider must declare
  (developer.android.com/develop/ui/views/appwidgets § "Determine widget sizing"):

      2 cells → 110dp    3 cells → 180dp    4 cells → 250dp    5 cells → 320dp

  The card composes at its REAL size rather than at a declared bucket (`SizeMode.Exact`,
  see `ListingsWidget.kt`), so these are the range the user may drag inside, not a set of
  sizes the layout is drawn for. Which BLOCKS a given height can afford is derived at
  composition time by `visibleBlocks` rather than declared here.
-->
<resources>
  <!--
    Default placement: 4 cells wide by 3 tall — the size at which the card shows
    everything it has to say (price, place, specs and the eyebrow), which is the one worth
    meeting the widget as.
  -->
  <dimen name="homiio_listings_widget_min_width">250dp</dimen>
  <dimen name="homiio_listings_widget_min_height">180dp</dimen>

  <!--
    How small the user may drag it: 2 cells by 2.

    Everything on this card is SHORT — a price, a place, a spec line — so a small card is
    not one that cannot do its job, it is one that shows fewer of those lines.
    `visibleBlocks` drops them in priority order and never promises one that does not fit,
    so the degradation is honest at any size in this range.

    The VERTICAL floor is derived from where that degradation stops being honest. A single
    cell of height (72dp) leaves room for the price and nothing else — replayed against
    `visibleBlocks`: 72dp less the 8dp the host keeps, less 24dp of padding, less a 24dp
    price line, leaves 16dp against the 21.6dp a place line and its gap need. And a rent
    with no location attached to it is not a listing, it is a number: a reader glancing at
    "€1,200/mo" learns nothing they can act on. So the floor is the next cell up, 110dp,
    where the price, the place AND the spec line all fit.

    `ListingsCardStyleTest` READS this value out of this file and asserts exactly that, so
    lowering it without re-deriving fails the build rather than shipping a card that shows
    a price over an unnamed home.

    Horizontally 110dp is fine: the place line ellipsizes against a width the `TextView`
    measures, so a narrow card shortens it rather than losing it.
  -->
  <dimen name="homiio_listings_widget_min_resize_width">110dp</dimen>
  <dimen name="homiio_listings_widget_min_resize_height">110dp</dimen>

  <!--
    The ceiling is where the card runs out of content to reveal. Price, place, specs and
    provenance is everything one listing has to say at a glance, and the photograph is the
    BACKGROUND — a taller or wider placement re-crops the same picture rather than showing
    more of the listing, and at a fixed pixel budget (`BACKGROUND_MAX_PIXELS`) a larger
    card only spreads those pixels thinner.
  -->
  <dimen name="homiio_listings_widget_max_resize_width">320dp</dimen>
  <dimen name="homiio_listings_widget_max_resize_height">320dp</dimen>
</resources>
